  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Using Index controllers, when putting your thumb on the touchpad or joystick, it will only consider the thumb as being down when pulling the joystick towards yourself or if touching the lower part of the touchpad. On the contrary, when pushing the joystick away from yourself or touching the upper part of the touchpad, the thumb will be considered as up. When in neutral position on the joystick or touchpad, the gesture will always be Idle.\n\nOld behaviour as the the thumb was always considered down if touching the joystick or touchpad no matter how or where. This new behaviour makes fist and pointing gestures much harder to perform.\n\nHappens with Legacy Fingers on OR off. \n\nUsing default Valve Index bindings from build Aug. 16.\n\nDisabling the skeleton in the bindings does restore old behaviour but that has its own issues obviously.\n\nVideo: https://files.catbox.moe/ehcq5p.mp4",
